# Round pp039: MiniMax-M3.1's host prompt leg is the NVFP4 planes tile's instructions. Lever A: the tile dots the
# offset codes (w + 12, MXFP4's unsigned side) against the column's codes as they are, and takes each column's
# 16-value code sums off in integers from a prep built once a call (qdot::dot_nvfp4_planes_rows_cols), so the per-column
# sign fold and the per-column scale build leave the inner loop; bit-identical to the one-column kernel. With it,
# walk039's 256-row prompt unit (place::PROMPT_ROWS and its prefill_units_full clause, byte-identical to 9e20c03e3),
# without which A sits under the DRAM line; and M3.1's admit floor held as a share of the unit's rows
# (gpu-minimaxm3 stream.rs STREAM_FLOOR = 32 x PROMPT_ROWS / 128 = 64): at 32 a 256-row unit halved the share an
# expert needs to be admitted, which is walk039's decode +3.2 % at D = 512, -3.5 % at 4096 and its admit at 4096
# 1.19 -> 1.65..2.85 s [d from m: ab-walk039.log against speed039's off arm].
#
