# 442,368 128-value groups an expert [derived, /Users/hckim/.cache/bloomery/placegen/pp039-decomp.md]:
#   tile per group of a row, run of C columns: base 65/101/135/169/201/234/267/324 instructions [asm, walk039];
#   this tree 30 + 22 C (C >= 2) [counted from the source]; FP-pipe uops base 28 + 27 C, this tree 24 + 21 C.
#   over Poisson column counts (balanced runs here, runs of 8 in base): 7.23 -> 5.09 G instructions a 128 rows at
#   T = 128 (0.70; uops 0.80), 7.00 -> 4.67 G at T = 256 (0.67; uops 0.79) [derived, pp039_model.py].
#   host DRAM: 21.3 ms a 128 rows at T = 128 (3.03 GB at 142 GB/s), 10.8 ms at T = 256.
#   base wall 22.13 ms a 128-row unit-layer (pp512 101.47 off) [m: probe-m31-xstream.log]; T = 256 alone measured
#   -0.5 % pp512 [m: ab-walk039.log], so the union is compute-bound at both T, R = 318..335 G instr/s.
#   A alone at T = 128: the union falls to the DRAM line, 22.13 -> ~21.7 ms, +2..+5 %: under the shadow.
#   A + T = 256: compute 20.9..22.0 ms x 0.67..0.79 = 13.9..17.4 ms a 128 rows, over DRAM 10.8; wall + 0.4..0.65.
#   admit (the serving word on bp) at speed039's admit share: 0.65..0.9 s at P = 512 (walk 1 0.741 s [d from m,
